**Tier 2 Data Support Engineer – Remote (Pacific/Mountain Time)**  
**Salary Range:** $81,000–$100,000 USD (All Other US Locations) | $93,000–$110,000 USD (SF Bay Area/NYC)  

**Overview:**  
Join Komodo Health’s Customer Support team to solve complex data challenges using SQL, Python, and your expertise in US healthcare data. As a Tier 2 Data Support Engineer, you will act as a technical detective—investigating, analyzing, and resolving advanced customer inquiries while partnering with engineering and product teams to ensure data integrity and drive healthcare innovation.

**Key Responsibilities:**  
- Investigate and resolve complex data issues using SQL (Snowflake) and Python.  
- Serve as the primary technical contact for Tier 2 support tickets from triage to resolution.  
- Communicate findings clearly to both technical and non-technical stakeholders.  
- Contribute to internal knowledge bases and customer documentation.  
- Collaborate cross-functionally to diagnose root causes and recommend product/process improvements.  
- Identify data trends and partner with Tier 3/backend teams for escalations.  
- Leverage AI tools to accelerate investigations, improve communications, and automate documentation.  

**Qualifications:**  
- Strong SQL skills (Snowflake preferred) and proficiency in Python.  
- Experience with US healthcare data (e.g., claims, EHR).  
- Analytical problem-solver with excellent communication skills.  
- Ability to manage competing priorities independently.  
- Collaborative team player with cross-functional experience.  
- Familiarity with ticketing systems (e.g., Jira Service Management, Zendesk) a plus.  
- Knowledge of cloud platforms (AWS preferred) a plus.  

**About Komodo Health:**  
Komodo Health’s mission is to reduce the global burden of disease by harnessing the power of the Healthcare Map—an industry-leading, de-identified patient data platform. We help clients uncover critical insights to improve patient outcomes and drive healthcare innovation.

**Benefits:**  
Comprehensive health, dental, and vision coverage, 401(k) with company match, paid time off, life and disability insurance, flexible work model, and equity opportunities.
